  "conclusion": "NOTHING SURVIVES.  Over 21 transformations of P_A, mpmath.identify returned no hit against any of 15 explicit bases at any of 3 tolerances (1e-44, 1e-40, 1e-36) with maxcoeff 1e5.  The PSLQ subset sweeps -- 64 jobs in total: 21 transformations x {1,2,3} named constants drawn from a 55-constant pool (55 + 1485 + 26235 = 27775 subsets each), plus one deliberately over-permissive sweep at maxcoeff 1e16 -- produced ZERO raw relations, so there was nothing even to apply the over-determination test to.  P_A is additionally not rational with numerator/denominator below 1e24, and not algebraic of degree <= 8 within the stated per-degree coefficient bounds.  The identical pipeline recovers all three calibration constants of known closed form (1, 2 and 3 named constants respectively), so this negative is meaningful and not a broken tool.",
